codex
The end-to-end symbolic proof now closes for all integers. I also matched Python’s empty-range behavior for negative inputs (`string_sequence(-3) == ""`), so the implementation agrees with the natural `range(n + 1)` interpretation beyond the prompt’s positive examples. I’m packaging the exact successful compile/run/prove sequence and doing one clean replay.
